  "title": "September 19 Weekly Observation — NVIDIA Throne 7 consecutive days of stability",
  "summary": "NVIDIA maintained the position of the sun at $5.37 trillion market cap, a week in which the order of the universe operated stably.",
  "body": "<h3>Stable Rule of the Sun</h3><p>Last week at the Universe Observatory, NVIDIA was recorded holding the Throne with a market cap of $5.37 trillion. Without a change of Throne compared to the previous week, the current Sovereign fully maintained its position, which means the order of the universe is maintaining a steady orbit. Apple ($4.91T) and Alphabet ($4.21T) follow, with the arrangement of the top 5 planets remaining stable.</p><h3>Active Fluctuations in Peripheral Planets</h3><p>While the center remains stable, notable changes were observed in the periphery of the universe. AMD (+8.5%) and Micron Technology (+4.2%) led the week's upward trend, with active orbital movements of semiconductor and memory industry planets detected. Meanwhile, Samsung Electronics (-2.7%), Saudi Aramco (-2.2%), and JPMorgan Chase (-1.8%) showed a downward trend for the week.</p><h3>Detection of New Signals</h3><p>The observatory's advanced equipment detected signs of the rise of an emerging planet called Arm Holdings. While entry into the major orbital zone has not yet occurred, it is necessary to monitor future movements. Additionally, Sandisk (712), Dell (330), and Seagate Technology (296) show high momentum, suggesting multi-layered changes in the universe.</p><h3>Observation Record</h3><p>In this week's observation, there were no rank changes among the top 5 planets, and no new entries or exits of planets were recorded. The universe continues to turn, and the observation records of each day remain.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"700\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#10141f\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#f2ba3c\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"800\">This week's stars — ignited stars and cooled stars</text><text x=\"26\"